      en: "The oldest surviving fort on New Providence. Built in 1741. Guards the eastern entrance to Nassau Harbour. Thus, the site is among the characteristic points of the Bahamas and offers insight into the regional identity of the archipelago. Located in the Caribbean island nation of the Bahamas. The region is marked by a tropical-maritime climate. Accessible via the national transport network of the islands. Plays a role in the local economy and culture. Representative of the diversity of the Bahamian landscape."
